sentences.text:
As per section 2 of Protection of Women from Domestic Violence Act, 2005;
2(a) "aggrrieved person" means any woman who is, or has been, in a domestic relationship with the respondent and who alleges to have been subjected to any act of domestic violence by the respondent;
2(s) "shared household" means a household where the person aggrieved lives or at any stage has lived in a domestic relationship either singly or along with the respondent and includes such a household whether owned or tenated either jointly by the aggrieved person and the respondent, or owned, or tenanted by either of then respondent, or owned or tenanted by either of then in respect of which either the aggrieved person or the respondent or both jointly orsingly have any right, title,
interest or equity and includes such a household which may belong to the joint family of which the respondent is a member, irrespective of whether the respondent or the aggrieved person has any right, title or interest in the Crl.Misc.No. 218/2016 shared household.
